{"content":"q26.\n\nThe following database tables are affected when `DeleteMemo` runs:\n\n1. **`memo_relation`** — Explicit cascade code in `store.Store.DeleteMemo` (`store/memo.go:142–146`) deletes rows where the memo is either `memo_id` or `related_memo_id`, via `Driver.DeleteMemoRelation` (SQL: `DELETE FROM memo_relation`, e.g. `store/db/sqlite/memo_relation.go:148–150`).\n\n2. **`attachment`** — Explicit cascade code in `store.Store.DeleteMemo` (`store/memo.go:149–156`) lists and deletes all attachments linked to the memo, via `Driver.DeleteAttachment` (SQL: `DELETE FROM attachment`, e.g. `store/db/sqlite/attachment.go:212`).\n\n3. **`memo`** — The memo row itself is deleted via `Driver.DeleteMemo` (SQL: `DELETE FROM memo`, e.g. `store/db/sqlite/memo.go:239`).\n\n4. **`memo_share`** — Via database-level `ON DELETE CASCADE` foreign key on `memo_id REFERENCES memo(id)` (`store/migration/sqlite/LATEST.sql:109`, and equivalent in MySQL/Postgres schemas).\n\nAdditionally, at the service layer (`server/router/api/v1/memo_service.go:567–577`), **comment memos** (found via `memo_relation` with type `Comment`) are recursively deleted by calling `Store.DeleteMemo` for each comment, which triggers the same cascade on all four tables above for each comment memo.\n\n**Table list:** `memo`, `memo_relation`, `attachment`, `memo_share`","iteration":10,"turn":1,"type":"assistant"}
